          </div>
          <span class="os-difficulty diff-medium">Thorough</span>
        </div>
        <div class="os-card-body">
          <ol class="os-steps">
            <li>Open the PDF in Acrobat Pro</li>
            <li>Go to Tools &rarr; Redact</li>
            <li>Click "Sanitize Document"</li>
            <li>Confirm and save the sanitized file</li>
            <li>Verify with ExifTool: <code>exiftool -Author document.pdf</code></li>
          </ol>
          <p style="margin-top:10px; font-size:12.5px; color:var(--ink-3);">Sanitize performs a complete PDF rewrite and is more reliable at XMP removal than the Properties editor. Still worth verifying after on critical documents.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="method-4-word-source">Method 4 &mdash; Fix the source in Word (prevents future exposure)</h2>

    <p>If you export a lot of documents from Word, fixing the source name means you never have to strip it from individual files. This changes what gets written into future PDFs &mdash; it doesn't fix existing files.</p>

    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy</button>
      <span class="c-comment"># In Microsoft Word:</span><br>
      <span class="c-comment"># File &rarr; Options &rarr; General &rarr; Personalize your copy of Microsoft Office</span><br>
      <span class="c-comment"># Change "User name" to your preferred value or leave blank</span><br><br>
      <span class="c-comment"># To clear Author from a specific document's properties:</span><br>
      <span class="c-comment"># File &rarr; Info &rarr; Properties (right panel) &rarr; click "Remove Personal Information"</span><br>
      <span class="c-comment"># OR: File &rarr; Info &rarr; Check for Issues &rarr; Inspect Document</span><br>
      <span class="c-comment"># Then check "Document Properties and Personal Information" &rarr; Remove All</span>
    </div>

    <div class="callout amber">
      <div class="callout-label">&#9888; Word's "Remove Personal Information" trap</div>
      <p>Word has a "Remove Personal Information from file properties on save" option (File &rarr; Options &rarr; Trust Center &rarr; Privacy Options). Enabling it removes the Author from the <em>Word document</em> properties &mdash; but when you export to PDF, the PDF generator may still pull your name from your Office user settings and embed it in the output PDF. Always verify the exported PDF separately, not just the source Word file.</p>
    </div>

